<title>USA: American Retirement jumps after IPO.</title>
<headline>American Retirement jumps after IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of American Retirement Corp jumped 14 percent after the initial public offering of the company, which operates senior communities and provides home health care services for the elderly.</p>
<p>The stock jumped two to 16 from its IPO price of $14, making it the top rising stock on the New York Stock Exchange on a percentage basis.  The price was below an IPO range of $15 to $17.</p>
<p>The company offered 3.125 million shares. The company was established in 1978.</p>
